-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for CircleProperty and
-- H3Proof (doc/circle-torsors.pdf): one entry per declaration, naming the
-- definitions its step reads "by definition".  Kinds as in truncation.opens;
-- in addition:
--   Equiv, idEquiv, qinv: the identity equivalence in the base case of eqind;
--   Lp: the family of loops, the motive of the transport of a loop;
--   trans, ap, sym, subst, happly at refl: the computation of J at refl;
--   K(Z,1): EM1.K1 -> TrivG.K -> TrivG.img and KZ2Cohomology.Zab -> intAb
--     (library aliases; on binders over K1 also the etaV defect,
--     doc/etav-lock-diagnostic.txt);
--   NatRec.Contract.trd-H-def opens sym, trans: the recursive call of the
--     split H compared with H n (checker strategy, not a step of the text).
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens circle.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
